[00:00:00] In some sense Codex was an example of this.
[00:00:09] We were way behind Claude Code, and it seemed like
[00:00:12] a kind of crazy kamikaze mission to try to beat them
[00:00:16] with a coding app. The consensus is that this kind
[00:00:22] of thing never works, and you just move on to the next
[00:00:24] one. It's a fool's errand to try to win when someone
[00:00:28] else already has momentum in a particular product category.
[00:00:30] But we decided we thought it was really important.
[00:00:32] We asked a team to do it, and they performed a legitimate,
[00:00:37] unbelievable, very rare in the history of business
[00:00:41] thing. Now it is the product that most of the best
[00:00:47] coders I know use. That felt like an impossible thing,
[00:00:51] but if we hadn't asked the team, hey, we have a really
[00:00:54] important but extremely hard mission for you, it just
[00:00:56] wouldn't have happened.

